  "query_preview": "..Quick discussion due to ongoing severe and flash\nflood threat. Increasing moisture across southern and eastern Utah\nwill continue to bring the threat of flash flooding through at\nleast Friday, though the highest potential will be through\nThursday morning. Given trends in CAMS with shortwave troughs\nejecting across the area ahead of the parent low off the Pacific\nCoast, multiple rounds of strong convection with a heavy rain\nthreat will occur. A majority of CAMS solutions develop an area \nof thunderstorms with heavy rain across southwestern and south\ncentral Utah near to after midnight, becoming widespread across\neastern and southern Utah by late Wednesday morning, mainly east\nof I-15.\n\nThis threat will continue through at least late Wednesday night,\npotentially into Thursday morning as yet another shortwave trough\nejects across the region. \n\nAs the upper level low ejects across the Great Basin Friday into\nSaturday, drier conditions will build into the state from west to\neast. \n\nA Flood Watch for flash flooding has been issued for portions of\nsouthern and eastern Utah from late tonight through Thursday\nmorning. Depending on trends, this may need to be extended to\ninclude additional zones in the state and/or extended into at\nleast Thursday night by later shifts.",
